    "narrative": "Our strongest plays today center on **Tyler Freeman** (64.38) and **Masyn Winn** (61.81), both of whom benefit from favorable matchups against pitchers with xERAs north of 4.40. **Tyler Freeman** is our clear efficiency leader; despite the assumed #8 spot in the order dragging his score down, his high park factor (+14%) and the favorable SP skill rating (+11%) make him a primary contributor for this slate. Similarly, **Masyn Winn** faces Merrill Kelly, and with the pitching matchup tilting the scale by +19%, he remains an essential start despite the uncertainty surrounding the finalized lineup. **Dylan Beavers** (60.18) rounds out our top trio, as his platoon advantage and favorable park environment offset his mid-order positioning to provide the best value in our outfield.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Ryan Waldschmidt**, who narrowly missed the cut with a 47.57 score. While his base projection was solid, the assumption of him batting #9 in the lineup resulted in a significant penalty, ultimately keeping him out of the starting nine in favor of higher-order hitters like **Gavin Sheets** and **Daulton Varsho**. Elsewhere, we are cautious about the start for **Jonathan Aranda** (51.26); while his xwOBA remains attractive, the -12% platoon penalty against a left-handed pitcher makes him a marginal play. We also see risk with **Cal Raleigh** (54.81), whose score is suppressed by a negative park factor and an adverse platoon split; however, his necessity as a foundational piece of our lineup mandates his inclusion. \n\nAll starters are currently under \"Lineup Pending\" status, which introduces non-trivial risk regarding our projected batting order assumptions. Owners should monitor weather reports and official cards, as any unexpected benching for **Taylor Ward** or **Lawrence Butler** would necessitate an immediate shift to our bench depth. While **Yainer Diaz** (39.26) and **Luis Arraez** (43.71) remain available on the bench, both are currently suppressed by elite pitching matchups against Dean Kremer and Bryce Miller, respectively, further validating our decision to lean into the matchups presented by **Tyler Freeman** and **Masyn Winn**.",
